From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucaszhongsj <lucaszhongsj@foxmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 02:40:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ios: a standing phone's picture fills the upper half

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: a phone standing up asked for a 1.43 picture while the upper half is
0.92, so the picture was cropped to fill that half; it now asks for the half's
own shape and is fitted, never cropped or stretched, and a touch's y maps back
onto the 16:9 interface the game draws centred there. A cold start lying down
takes the screen's shape from the scene's orientation, which the screen's
bounds may still report the other way round.
Issue: none yet: no upstream issue for the iOS front end
